<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" version="2.0"><channel><title>Personal Combined Feed</title><link>https://example.invalid</link><description>Personal aggregate feed</description><docs>http://www.rssboard.org/rss-specification</docs><generator>python-feedgen</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 07:28:06 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>Ask HN: How do you use AI for building in public?</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50002798</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Fellow founders, I know AI writing is strictly forbidden here. But I was wondering if yall hand write every single post on X or on Linkedin for ship updates or user engagement posts. 
For small team like mine, I'm in charge of my own account. Not gonna lie, content batching and writing everything from scratch are extra work for me. 
On the other side, when I outsource my content generation to AI, my personality gets washed away. 
I'm curious how other founders approach this. 
Do you use AI to some extent for content batching,  drafting or editing? How do you draw the line?&lt;/p&gt;
